Create the API endpoint to receive webhook callbacks from Apify when actors complete.

## Endpoint
`POST /api/webhooks/hashtag-monitor/apify`

## File
`app/api/webhooks/hashtag-monitor/apify/route.ts`

Note: This follows the pattern from the provider abstraction ticket which creates a dynamic `[provider]` route. This ticket is for the Apify-specific handling.

## Implementation

```typescript
import { NextRequest } from "next/server";
import { db } from "@/lib/db";
import { hashtagMentions } from "@/lib/db/schema";
import { apifyProvider } from "@/lib/hashtag-monitoring/providers/apify";
import { processIncomingPosts } from "@/lib/hashtag-monitoring/handler";

export async function POST(request: NextRequest) {
  // 1. Validate webhook secret
  const secret = request.headers.get("x-apify-secret");
  if (secret !== process.env.APIFY_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
    return Response.json({ error: "Unauthorized" }, { status: 401 });
  }

  // 2. Parse payload
  const payload = await request.json();

  // 3. Use provider to normalize data
  const posts = apifyProvider.parseWebhookPayload(payload);

  // 4. Process posts (save to DB, match users, trigger milestones)
  const result = await processIncomingPosts("apify", posts);

  return Response.json({
    success: true,
    processed: result.processed,
    matched: result.matched,
    duplicates: result.duplicates,
  });
}
```

## Payload Handling

Apify webhooks include:
- `resource.defaultDatasetId` - ID to fetch results
- Or direct results in body (depending on config)

May need to fetch dataset if not included:
```typescript
const datasetUrl = `https://api.apify.com/v2/datasets/${datasetId}/items`;
const response = await fetch(datasetUrl, {
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.APIFY_API_TOKEN}` }
});
const items = await response.json();
```

## Error Handling
- Log failed webhook processing
- Return 200 even on partial failure (to prevent Apify retries flooding)
- Store errors in a log table or external service

