- [ ] Handle normalization handles edge cases
- [ ] Multiple handles per platform supported
- [ ] Matched posts linked to user in database
- [ ] Milestone checking triggered for matched users
- [ ] Unmatched posts still saved (for potential future matching)

Create a provider-agnostic interface for hashtag monitoring services.

## Architecture

### Interface: lib/hashtag-monitoring/types.ts
```typescript
interface HashtagMonitoringProvider {
  name: string;
  // Process incoming webhook/callback data
  parseWebhookPayload(payload: unknown): ParsedPost[];
  // For polling-based providers
  fetchRecentPosts?(hashtag: string, since?: Date): Promise<ParsedPost[]>;
}

interface ParsedPost {
  platform: 'tiktok' | 'instagram' | 'youtube' | 'twitter' | 'facebook';
  postUrl: string;
  postId?: string;
  authorHandle: string;
  postedAt: Date;
  metadata?: { likes?: number; views?: number; };
}
```

### Provider Registry: lib/hashtag-monitoring/index.ts
- Register available providers
- Get provider by name
- Route webhooks to correct provider

### Handler: lib/hashtag-monitoring/handler.ts
- processIncomingPost(provider: string, payload: unknown)
- Match author handle to user (via tracking_hashtag or social handles)
- Create post record with source = provider name
- Call checkAndAwardMilestones()

